       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. STEPDMIX.
      *> THE STEP D ARM-1 DISSOLUTION (kb/Work PB164's LAST HALF) - A
      *> MIXED-USAGE REDEFINES CLASS IS AN ORDINARY TIER-B BYTE-WINDOW
      *> CLASS: EVERY LEAF OCCUPIES ITS PINNED NumericByteForm BYTES
      *> (13.18.44.4 GR1 - STORAGE ASSOCIATION AT THE BIT OVER "THE
      *> NUMBER OF BITS REQUIRED"; GR2 - ANY ENTRY'S NAME REFERENCES
      *> THAT STORAGE; THE ITEM 205/207/208/211 DETERMINATIONS). THE
      *> WINDOW BYTES ARE READ THROUGH THE REDEFINED X VIEW WITH
      *> FUNCTION ORD (15.70; NEVER A SELF-INVERSE ROUND TRIP): THE
      *> FULL-CONTAINER COMP-5 (FF FF), THE IEEE COMP-1 (3F C0 00 00),
      *> THE R40 INDEX OCCURRENCE (BYTE 14 = 03), THE UNSIGNED-WIDE
      *> 9(10) COMP-5 (BYTE 18 = 01 FOR 2^32). THE WRITE-THROUGH LEG
      *> THEN PUTS "AB" THROUGH THE VIEW: THE COMP-5 MEMBER DECODES
      *> 16706 (0x4142) - DISPLAYED AS ITS R13 PICTURE-DIGIT IMAGE
      *> (6706, THE MOD-10^4 OWNER DECISION - IDENTICAL TO A NATIVE
      *> COMP-5), WHILE THE MOVE PATH (14.9.25.4 GR6d) CARRIES THE
      *> FULL VALUE INTO A 9(5) RECEIVER. ONE STORAGE, TWO
      *> DESCRIPTIONS, AND THE WINDOWED MEMBER BEHAVES EXACTLY AS
      *> ITS NATIVE TWIN WOULD.
      *>
      *> THE STEP D REVIEW WAVE ADDED THE FOUR EMIT LANES THE FIRST
      *> PASS LEFT UNOBSERVED, EACH AGAINST A NATIVE CONTROL - THE
      *> POINT IS ALWAYS THAT THE TWO PRINT THE SAME TEXT, BECAUSE
      *> 13.18.44.4 GR1 GIVES THEM ONE STORAGE AND 14.9.11.4 GR1
      *> LEAVES ONLY THE *FORM* OF THE TEXT TO THE IMPLEMENTOR:
      *>   WF/NF  DISPLAY OF A WINDOWED FLOAT. IT PRINTED THE RAW IEEE
      *>          BYTES (3F C0 00 00) INSTEAD OF 1.5 - A SILENT WRONG
      *>          ANSWER, BECAUSE THE DECODE LANE EXCLUDED IsFloat.
      *>   CV     FUNCTION CONVERT SOURCE-FORMAT ANY (15.19.3 r7 -
      *>          "argument-1 shall be of any usage ... It is not
      *>          necessary for the contents to be valid according to
      *>          the usage"), THE ITEM'S STORAGE BITS AS HEX. THE
      *>          WINDOWED ARM WAS A BACKEND CS1503.
      *>   UW/UB  A 16-BYTE UNSIGNED COMP-5 WINDOW OF ALL X"FF" =
      *>          2^128-1. ITS 31-DIGIT PICTURE IMAGE IS
      *>          6920938463463374607431768211455; A SIGNED DECODE
      *>          PRINTED ...0001 INSTEAD. UB THEN RE-ENCODES IT AND
      *>          READS THE BYTES BACK: THE ROUND TRIP MUST BE EXACT
      *>          (IT CAME BACK 00..01 - THE UNSIGNED CARRIER WAS
      *>          TAKING 14.9.25.4 GR6b'S ABSOLUTE VALUE OF A
      *>          REINTERPRETED BIT PATTERN).
      *>   IZ     INITIALIZE INTO THE WINDOW (14.9.20 GR4'S IMPLICIT
      *>          MOVE). THE FLOAT LEG SPLICED A float INTO A string
      *>          WINDOW - ANOTHER CS1503.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-T.
          05 WS-E PIC X OCCURS 9 INDEXED BY IX.
       01 G.
          05 G-C5 PIC 9(4) COMP-5.
          05 G-F  USAGE COMP-1.
          05 G-IX USAGE INDEX.
          05 G-W  PIC 9(10) COMP-5.
       01 R REDEFINES G PIC X(22).
       01 WS-V5 PIC 9(5).
      *> THE NATIVE CONTROLS - SAME DESCRIPTIONS, NO REDEFINES.
       01 N-F  USAGE COMP-1.
       01 WS-H  PIC X(8).
       01 WS-H2 PIC X(8).
      *> THE 16-BYTE UNSIGNED PAIR: ONE WINDOW TO SET, ONE TO RE-ENCODE
      *> INTO, SO THE BYTES CAN BE READ BACK THROUGH ITS OWN X VIEW.
       01 GU.
          05 GU-W  PIC 9(31) COMP-5.
       01 RU REDEFINES GU PIC X(16).
       01 GU2.
          05 GU2-W PIC 9(31) COMP-5.
       01 RU2 REDEFINES GU2 PIC X(16).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE 65535 TO G-C5
           MOVE 1.5 TO G-F
           SET IX TO 3
           SET G-IX TO IX
           MOVE 4294967296 TO G-W
           DISPLAY FUNCTION ORD(R(1:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(R(2:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(R(3:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(R(14:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(R(18:1))
           MOVE "AB" TO R(1:2)
           DISPLAY G-C5
           MOVE G-C5 TO WS-V5
           DISPLAY WS-V5
      *> WF/NF - THE WINDOWED FLOAT AND ITS NATIVE TWIN.
           MOVE 1.5 TO N-F
           DISPLAY "WF=[" G-F "] NF=[" N-F "]"
      *> CV - CONVERT ANY OVER BOTH, THE SAME IEEE STORAGE BITS.
           MOVE FUNCTION CONVERT(G-F ANY ANUM HEX) TO WS-H
           MOVE FUNCTION CONVERT(N-F ANY ANUM HEX) TO WS-H2
           DISPLAY "CV=[" WS-H "][" WS-H2 "]"
      *> UW/UB - THE 16-BYTE UNSIGNED WINDOW, READ THEN ROUND-TRIPPED.
           MOVE ALL X"FF" TO RU
           DISPLAY "UW=[" GU-W "]"
           MOVE GU-W TO GU2-W
           DISPLAY "UB=" FUNCTION ORD(RU2(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(RU2(8:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RU2(16:1))
      *> IZ - INITIALIZE THROUGH THE WINDOW (LAST: IT CLEARS G).
           INITIALIZE G
           DISPLAY "IZ=[" G-C5 "][" G-F "][" G-W "]"
           STOP RUN.
